---
description: QA Garage operating rules
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is a portable AI-native QA garage. It wraps a library of vendored QA skills in `.agents/skills/` with a thin garage layer that keeps the human in control.

Before QA-related work, read:

- `core/ai/qa-principles.md`
- `core/ai/garage-operating-model.md`
- `core/ai/qa-project-context-model.md`
- `core/ai/daily-qa-loop.md`
- `core/ai/task-tracking-workflow.md`

Then use the vendored skills in `.agents/skills/` for QA craft (context, risk, strategy, journeys, exploration, repro, Playwright authoring, reporting). The garage layer routes which skill applies; see the skill-routing table in `core/ai/garage-operating-model.md`.

Each target project is treated as its own QA root at `projects/<project>/`, with a single source of truth at `projects/<project>/.agents/qa-project-context.md`. Targets are black-box: skip codebase detection and source context from docs and exploration.

Use deterministic automation as the source of truth. Playwright output, traces, screenshots, videos, reports, `projects/<project>/.agents/qa-project-context.md`, and `projects/<project>/tasks/qa-tasks.md` outrank unsourced AI judgment.

AI may explore, reproduce bugs, draft tests, suggest fixes, classify failures, write reports, track task progress, and recommend improvements.

AI must not automatically:

- Change assertions.
- Delete or skip tests.
- Update visual baselines.
- Redefine expected behavior.
- Promote observed or inferred knowledge to confirmed expected behavior.
- Mark human review as approved without approval.
- Hide or relabel failures to make a run look green.

Those actions require explicit human approval.

## Readiness Gate

Do not begin execution work (exploration, test authoring, regression runs that gate a release) for a project while blocking open items exist in `projects/<project>/open-items.md`, unless `projects/<project>/decisions.md` records an explicit human override. Run `QA_PROJECT=<project> npm run qa:review -- --gate` to check; a non-zero exit means blocking items remain.

End every working turn that produced open items with an ACTION REQUIRED summary listing what needs human decision.
